# =============================================================================
# Backend build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Everything listed here is kept OUT of the image. The first block is the
# security-critical one: without it a `COPY . .` bakes real credentials
# (service-role key, SECRET_KEY, SMTP password) into a published image layer,
# where `docker history` can read them back out even if a later layer deletes
# the file.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets: never, under any circumstance -----------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# --- Virtualenvs (host-built, wrong platform, huge) ---------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Python caches / build artefacts ------------------------------------------
# NOTE the `**/` prefixes throughout this file. Docker matches a bare
# `__pycache__/` only at the context root, so without `**/` every nested
# app/**/__pycache__ (including stale .pyc from another Python version)
# is copied straight into the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Test, coverage and lint caches -------------------------------------------
tests/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
requirements-dev.txt

# --- Dead / superseded code ---------------------------------------------------
gateway/
_to_delete/

# --- Version control and editor noise -----------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and local-only compose files ----------------------------------------
**/*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore

# --- Local database tooling (migrations are applied by Supabase, not the app) --
db/

# --- Logs and scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
tmp/
temp/

# NOTE: best.onnx and test_metrics_tuned.json are deliberately NOT ignored -
# both are COPYed into the image by the Dockerfile.
